  "result": "Perfect! All 130 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented for VAT:\n\n**VAT Calculation Implementation**\n\n\u2705 **src/invoices.js updates:**\n- Added `lineVAT(line)` function: calculates VAT as `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) * vatRate / 100`, rounded with `roundCents()`\n  - VAT is computed per line on the discounted amount\n  - Each line VAT is rounded independently\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where:\n  - `subtotal` = sum of line totals\n  - `discount` = sum of line discounts\n  - `vat` = sum of independently rounded line VATs\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n\u2705 **src/render.js updates:**\n- Now displays VAT line when `vat > 0`\n- VAT line appears just above the Total line\n- Format: `VAT: \u20acamount` (like Discount: -\u20acamount)\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests (18 new VAT tests):**\n- lineVAT calculations with various rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n- VAT on discounted amounts\n- VAT rounding (banker's rounding)\n- invoiceTotals with VAT, discounts, tier discounts combined\n- invoiceTotals with mixed VAT rates\n- renderInvoiceText showing/hiding VAT lines\n- VAT line position (above total)\n- VAT with discount combinations\n\nKey design decisions:\n- VAT computed per line on discounted amount (subtotal - discount)\n- Each line's VAT rounded independently before summing\n- Invoice VAT is never a percentage of total (sum of rounded line VATs)\n- Clamping total at 0 applies after adding VAT, so total never negative\n\nAll 130 tests passing.",
